 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$. The computation involves a fixed number of arithmetic operations, square roots, and comparisons.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$. No auxiliary data structures are needed.
-*   **Strengths:** Exact distance calculation allows for large step sizes in ray marching, improving performance. Smooth gradients (except at the base edge and apex) allow for accurate normal computation.
-*   **Limitations:** The function is not differentiable at the base edge (where the side slope meets the base cap) and at the apex. This can cause artifacts in normal-based shading or physics if not handled.
-*   **When to use:** When rendering conical objects with high precision is required, or when using the SDF for collision detection where exact boundaries matter.
-*   **When not to use:** If the cone is part of a complex mesh where polygonal approximation is sufficient and faster, or if the cone is extremely long and thin, where precision issues might arise.
